    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for 2026-07-09 is defined by high-ceiling matchups against soft-tossing rotations. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Cole Carrigg** (70.41) anchor the outfield, representing our strongest starts of the day. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a lucrative matchup against Merrill Kelly (5.37 xERA) and the benefit of a clean order position, while **Cole Carrigg** is the day\u2019s high-leverage play; he faces Whisenhunt in a favorable park environment with wind blowing out, boosting his base projection significantly. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** (69.47) and **Jacob Wilson** (68.72) provide elite stability in the middle infield, as both capitalize on the vulnerabilities of their respective left-handed opponents.\n\nPlatoon advantages and environmental factors remain the primary drivers for our daily lineup composition. **Heliot Ramos** (66.63) sees a double-digit boost thanks to a lead-off spot against Feltner and wind assistance, while **Coby Mayo** (66.72) is a strong play at first base, thriving despite the slight \"Elite Hold\" penalty associated with stolen base prevention. Conversely, we are exercising caution with **Liam Hicks** (42.26); his lead-off spot and platoon leverage are offset by a daunting matchup against Miller, whose 2.44 xERA necessitates a more conservative start to protect game caps. **Josh Jung** (48.12) and **Nolan Schanuel** (46.84) round out our lower-tier starters, both facing challenging arms but retaining enough positional value to keep them in the mix.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's bench was **Miguel Vargas** (42.35). While his xwOBA of 0.403 suggests elite contact quality, the efficiency model penalized him heavily for facing Sandoval (2.08 xERA), ultimately favoring the higher-floor matchups of our active roster. **Wade Meckler**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Denzer Guzman** were all considered but ultimately sat due to failing to clear the \"Zebras Floor\" of 40.0; their profiles, lacking the raw efficiency needed to displace our primary starters, remain in reserve. We are monitoring all lineups closely for late changes, but provided the current conditions hold, we are well-positioned to chase production in the stolen base and batting average categories.",
